{
  "generated_text": "To determine the number of shirt-and-tie outfits that can be made while ensuring that a shirt and a tie are not of the same color, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of choices for shirts and ties:**\n   - There are 8 colors, and for each color, there is one shirt and one tie.\n   - Therefore, there are 8 choices for shirts and 8 choices for ties.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of possible shirt-and-tie outfits without any restrictions:**\n   - If there were no restrictions, the total number of outfits would be the product of the number of choices for shirts and the number of choices for ties.\n   \\[\n   8 \\text{ (shirts)} \\times 8 \\text{ (ties)} = 64 \\text{ outfits}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Identify the restricted outfits:**\n   - A restricted outfit is one where the shirt and tie are of the same color.\n   - Since there are 8 colors, there are 8 restricted outfits (one for each color).\n\n4. **Calculate the number of unrestricted outfits:**\n   - To find the number of unrestricted outfits, subtract the number of restricted outfits from the total number of outfits.\n   \\[\n   64 \\text{ (total outfits)} - 8 \\text{ (restricted outfits)} = 56 \\text{ (unrestricted outfits)}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of shirt-and-tie outfits that can be made, ensuring that a shirt and a tie are not of the same color, is \\(\\boxed{56}\\).",
